<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamar of Georgia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1160–<a href="/years/1213">1213</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Queen Tamar, Tamar the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamar was queen regnant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1184 to 1213, and her reign marks the height of the medieval Georgian kingdom. Her second husband, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-soslan">David Soslan</a>, was an Alanian prince. Her armies won at Shamkor and Basian, took Ani in 1199 and helped found the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a>, and the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shota-rustaveli">Shota Rustaveli</a> dedicated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-knight-in-the-panthers-skin">The Knight in the Panther's Skin</a> to her.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia.jpg" alt="Tamar of Georgia" width="320" height="587" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 13th century painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betania_Monastery,_Tamar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
